Fertilizers Europe. Guidance for the Storage, Handling, and Transportation of Solid Mineral Fertilizers, issue 2015. [Association record](https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/publications/guidance-for-the-storage-handling-and-transportation-of-solid-mineral-fertilizers/) · [Complete guide](https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/Final-version-Storage-handling-and-transport-of-solid-fertilizers-18112015.pdf).

Read the whole guide for the solid-feed project, following product differences, storage, contamination, physical change and transfers between manufacturers, distributors and users. Use the exact formulation and analysis basis when connecting nutrient identity with mass handled and service provided.

The complete 100-file-page document's identity, contents and notice were inspected on 29 October 2026. It distinguishes the 2007 edition from the 2015 issue; the URL directory alone is insufficient to date it. Preserve its Fertilizers Europe copyright and dated technical/regulatory scope. In particular, the guidance excludes liquid, organic/organo-mineral fertilisers and non-fertiliser forms of ammonium nitrate. Referenced standards keep their own rights. No full text, image or table is copied.

